<h1>internal node</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="node.html"><em>node</em></a> of a <a href="tree.html"><em>tree</em></a> that has one or more <a href="child.html"><em>child</em></a> nodes, equivalently, one that is not a <a href="leaf.html"><em>leaf</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Also known as</strong> nonterminal node.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="parent.html"><em>parent</em></a>, <a href="root.html"><em>root</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
See <a href="../terms.html#CLR90">[CLR90, page 93]</a> or <a href="../terms.html#HS83">[HS83, page 220]</a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Authors: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorLJW">LJW</a>,<a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

<hr>

